<title>PORTUGAL: INSTANT VIEW-Cimpor could gain on Brazil.</title>
<headline>INSTANT VIEW-Cimpor could gain on Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are reactions from stock analysts to news that Cimpor-Cimentos de Portugal bought two cement companies in Brazil -- Companhia de Cimento de Sao Francisco-Cisafra and the cement interests of the Serrana group.</p>
<p>JOSE FREIRE, ESPIRITO SANTO RESEARCH</p>
<p>&quot;I think that Cimpor stock could gain. The (Brazilian) companies were bought at a reasonable price.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;I think that Cimpor could go to 4.000 escudos&quot;.  </p>
<p>PEDRO ASSUNCAO, CENTRAL DE INVESTIMENTOS</p>
<p>&quot;I think that the (share) price of Cimpor was already anticipating a bit these purchases. Nevertheless, the investment is significantly more than was expected but the increase in (production) capacity is pretty positive for the company.</p>
<p>&quot;The price seems reasonable&quot;.</p>
<p>--Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
